  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Women, Peace and Security (Global) 2022-2027</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The WPS Investment (2022-2027) is one significant and substantial means through which DFAT contributes to achieving the goal of Australia&#x2019;s second National Action Plan on Women, Peace and Security 2021-2031: that in the context of increasing insecurity with climate change, diverse women and girls realise their human rights and achieve meaningful participation to prevent and resolve conflict and establish enduring peace.

The investment includes support to:
(i) the Women&#x2019;s Peace and Humanitarian Fund;
(ii) UN Women&#x2019;s Regional Framework Towards Peaceful, Inclusive Societies in the Asia-Pacific;
(iii) the Southeast Asian Women Peace Mediators;
(iv) the Pacific Women Mediator&#x2019;s Network; and to strengthen civil society engagement on WPS among women peacebuilders in Asia, the Pacific and Great Lakes region of Africa; and  
(v) the creation of a global Gender Justice Practitioner Hub to support and connect practitioners involved in securing gender justice for core international crimes.</narrative>
  </description>
